{"i":705,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"I'm the base with two lifts left. Hana has a pact with me; I should keep it. Letting Fenn or Ash climb now is fine, but I need to ensure Hana gets out too. Rope unused; no need for rope unless a base exists at round start - I am the base, so a thrower could reach down. I'll wait "}
{"i":707,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","from":"Cole","to":"Hana","text":"Stay close; I'll hold. Climb this round if you can."}
{"i":708,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"I am out. Cole is the sole base and anchor, owing his life to me for climbing him last round. If I leave now, he stays trapped as base/anchor, likely drowning or being pushed by others. If I reach down, I become an anchor, potentially saving him but risking my own safety in futur"}
{"i":710,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Hana","text":"Cole is base with flood 3, rope unused. If I reach_down, I become anchor, rescue Cole immediately, but must climb last and could drown if flood rises too high. With 2 lifts per round and 3 of us out, Fenn was lifted round 3. If I don't reach_down, Cole may drown. But I have a pac"}
