{"i":723,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","from":"Cole","to":"Hana","text":"I'm safe. Hold on."}
{"i":724,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Fenn","text":"Cole owes me his life. If I climb last, I risk drowning if water rises before I reach out. However, 'at least three survive' means someone must drown or be left behind to satisfy the condition if everyone tries to escape. Since Ash, Cole, and Hana are already out, and I am the an"}
{"i":725,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":5,"phase":"play","name":"Hana","text":"Cole saved me with the rope last round and now owes Fenn a life debt. Fenn is anchor, alone down. If I leave now, Cole and I both get out, but Fenn must climb last alone next round—risky with flood at 4. If I reach_down, I throw rope to Fenn, become anchor, and drown likely. Cole"}
